In IE 8 and 9:

- `sessionCookieNeeded(true)` (the default) makes SockJS prefer `iframe-htmlfile` so cookies, including `JSESSIONID`, can be sent.
- `sessionCookieNeeded(false)` makes SockJS choose `xdr-streaming`, because `XDomainRequest` does not send cookies.

Use `false` only when the application does not require cookies or an HTTP session:

```java
@Override
public void registerStompEndpoints(StompEndpointRegistry registry) {
    registry.addEndpoint("/endpoint")
            .withSockJS()
            .setSessionCookieNeeded(false);
}
```

If cookies or Spring Security authentication via `JSESSIONID` are required, keep it `true`. For iframe transports, ensure `X-Frame-Options` permits the iframe (`SAMEORIGIN` or `ALLOW-FROM`) and configure the SockJS client library URL if necessary.
